1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,783
For eight lectures, you've drawn every floor your crew walked on.

2
00:00:06,583 --> 00:00:08,757
Today they board a ship,

3
00:00:09,207 --> 00:00:10,946
and you draw nothing.

4
00:00:11,846 --> 00:00:15,759
The game builds her deck from her own plan,

5
00:00:16,209 --> 00:00:18,383
and puts her crew aboard.

6
00:00:20,183 --> 00:00:22,791
Your job is what's on it.

7
00:00:23,691 --> 00:00:27,170
A prisoner, a gunner who won't give up,

8
00:00:27,620 --> 00:00:31,098
and a strongbox that ends it three ways.

9
00:00:32,898 --> 00:00:38,985
One warning first: this is brand new, and three things about it are rough.

10
00:00:39,885 --> 00:00:42,059
I'll show you each one.

11
00:00:43,259 --> 00:00:45,433
The button needs four things.

12
00:00:46,333 --> 00:00:48,507
A ship that has struck.

13
00:00:48,957 --> 00:00:51,130
A hull with a plan.

14
00:00:51,580 --> 00:00:55,059
The station art, which your starter already has.

15
00:00:56,859 --> 00:00:59,033
And no other party out.

16
00:00:59,933 --> 00:01:02,541
That last one is the trouble.

17
00:01:04,341 --> 00:01:07,820
Your relay party opens in the first second,

18
00:01:08,270 --> 00:01:12,617
and a party on a map never closes by itself.

19
00:01:13,517 --> 00:01:15,691
So as your mission stands,

20
00:01:16,141 --> 00:01:18,315
nobody could ever board her.

21
00:01:20,115 --> 00:01:22,724
We fix that with one rule.

22
00:01:23,174 --> 00:01:26,652
When she strikes, the landing party comes home.

23
00:01:27,552 --> 00:01:31,465
When the ship comes back, the relay opens again.

24
00:01:32,665 --> 00:01:36,143
First, a side for her to be on.

25
00:01:36,593 --> 00:01:40,072
One record, and one line that says enemies.

26
00:01:41,872 --> 00:01:44,915
Then the ship, in the story file.

27
00:01:45,365 --> 00:01:48,409
Two lines, under the relay's own line.

28
00:01:50,209 --> 00:01:51,948
Look at the numbers.

29
00:01:52,848 --> 00:01:56,326
The first set is where she comes from.

30
00:01:56,776 --> 00:01:59,385
The second is where she is.

31
00:02:01,185 --> 00:02:06,837
That matters, because a ship that strikes and isn't boarded runs for home,

32
00:02:07,287 --> 00:02:11,635
and when she gets there she's taken off the map.

33
00:02:12,535 --> 00:02:15,143
I tried it with one place.

34
00:02:15,593 --> 00:02:19,507
She struck, and eight seconds later she was gone.

35
00:02:20,707 --> 00:02:22,880
There are three quests here.

36
00:02:23,780 --> 00:02:28,998
Run her down, which waits for the ship to close on her.

37
00:02:29,898 --> 00:02:34,246
Come back to the relay, which is hidden until then.

38
00:02:35,146 --> 00:02:39,928
And take her, which waits for a signal the game sends.

39
00:02:41,728 --> 00:02:45,641
Two of them get a page for the bridge.

40
00:02:46,091 --> 00:02:50,004
The brigantine drawn at the top of the chase,

41
00:02:50,454 --> 00:02:53,498
and two icon bullets on the prize.

42
00:02:55,298 --> 00:02:57,907
The card is one you know.

43
00:02:58,357 --> 00:03:01,835
It's the tug card from the first class,

44
00:03:02,285 --> 00:03:04,459
hearing a different step start.

45
00:03:06,259 --> 00:03:07,998
It does two things.

46
00:03:08,448 --> 00:03:12,361
It calls the landing party home, and she strikes.

47
00:03:14,161 --> 00:03:18,074
And the same line goes on your old card,

48
00:03:18,524 --> 00:03:20,263
for the trip back.

49
00:03:21,463 --> 00:03:23,637
Now the two new words.

50
00:03:24,537 --> 00:03:28,015
Area, deck: that means whatever ship we board.

51
00:03:29,815 --> 00:03:34,163
And mark is no longer a mark in a file,

52
00:03:34,613 --> 00:03:36,787
because there is no file.

53
00:03:37,687 --> 00:03:39,861
It's a kind of room.

54
00:03:40,311 --> 00:03:42,050
Brig, cargo, quarters, bay.

55
00:03:43,850 --> 00:03:46,893
Her hold is called the plunder hold.

56
00:03:47,343 --> 00:03:49,517
Her sickbay is the surgery.

57
00:03:50,417 --> 00:03:53,026
You don't need to know that.

58
00:03:53,476 --> 00:03:57,824
You write the kind, and it works on any hull.

59
00:03:59,624 --> 00:04:03,102
And when a hull has no such room,

60
00:04:03,552 --> 00:04:08,770
your thing stands in the hallway, and the game says so once.

61
00:04:09,970 --> 00:04:12,143
Here's the first rough thing.

62
00:04:13,943 --> 00:04:16,987
The game puts her own crew aboard,

63
00:04:17,437 --> 00:04:19,176
calm, and standing still.

64
00:04:20,076 --> 00:04:24,424
And a calm person blocks the cell they stand on.

65
00:04:26,224 --> 00:04:29,702
I put the strongbox in the captain's cabin.

66
00:04:30,152 --> 00:04:33,630
One of her crew stood inside the door.

67
00:04:34,530 --> 00:04:38,009
Nobody could reach it, and nothing said so.

68
00:04:39,809 --> 00:04:44,591
Worse, where they stand changes every time you add a record.

69
00:04:46,391 --> 00:04:48,565
So there are three rules.

70
00:04:49,465 --> 00:04:55,987
Put what the story needs in the brig, a bay, the entry or a hallway.

71
00:04:56,887 --> 00:04:59,496
A hostile is never shut in.

72
00:05:00,396 --> 00:05:02,135
And after every change,

73
00:05:02,585 --> 00:05:05,628
go aboard and walk to each thing.

74
00:05:06,828 --> 00:05:08,567
Now play it through.

75
00:05:09,467 --> 00:05:12,946
Helm closes to fifteen hundred, and she strikes.

76
00:05:13,846 --> 00:05:16,889
Comms selects her, and sends a party.

77
00:05:18,689 --> 00:05:22,167
Aboard, the strongbox has three answers that matter.

78
00:05:23,067 --> 00:05:26,111
Take her, and she joins your side,

79
00:05:26,561 --> 00:05:28,300
and the quest pays.

80
00:05:29,200 --> 00:05:31,374
Scuttle her, and she's gone.

81
00:05:32,274 --> 00:05:35,317
Leave her, and she runs for home.

82
00:05:37,117 --> 00:05:41,030
Every one of them brings the party home first.

83
00:05:41,930 --> 00:05:43,670
And after every one,

84
00:05:44,120 --> 00:05:48,033
the relay opens again when the ship comes back.

85
00:05:49,233 --> 00:05:51,841
The second rough thing is lint.

86
00:05:52,741 --> 00:05:55,350
Your finished mission shows two warnings,

87
00:05:55,800 --> 00:05:57,539
and both are wrong.

88
00:05:58,439 --> 00:06:01,483
So two is the number to check.

89
00:06:03,283 --> 00:06:05,891
The third you know from before.

90
00:06:06,341 --> 00:06:11,124
A full shot destroys any prop, and that includes the strongbox.

91
00:06:12,924 --> 00:06:16,402
Comms has its own button, take as prize.

92
00:06:16,852 --> 00:06:21,200
It skips everything you wrote, and the quest never pays.

93
00:06:23,000 --> 00:06:27,783
What the gunner drops is lost if nobody picks it up.

94
00:06:29,583 --> 00:06:33,930
And from her deck, the transporter still reaches your relay.

95
00:06:34,830 --> 00:06:37,874
Know these before your crew finds them.

96
00:06:39,074 --> 00:06:40,813
Now it's your turn.

97
00:06:41,713 --> 00:06:43,452
Play all three endings.

98
00:06:44,352 --> 00:06:49,135
Move the strongbox into the cabin, and try to reach it.

99
00:06:50,035 --> 00:06:54,817
Swap her hull for a freighter, and see where everything goes.

100
00:06:56,617 --> 00:07:00,096
Then light the beacon with the gunner's cell.

101
00:07:00,996 --> 00:07:04,039
Next time, the mission is your own.
